  <diagram id="vq-vae-architecture" name="Single-layer VQ-VAE">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1084" pageHeight="388" background="#ffffff" description="Illustrative vectors for the three token positions next, chess and match. The blue bars are original and reconstructed frozen-language-model activations. Amber bars are continuous encoder outputs. The quantizer replaces each of these with the nearest vector in the shared codebook. For chess, the quantizer assigns code 3. The teal bars show the vector stored for code 3, which is what the decoder receives. Bar height represents the value of one vector coordinate; values and assignments are illustrative, not measured." sourceUrl="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.02726v2"><root>
